    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d864">

                <pb facs="0911" n="823" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg823"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr.
                            Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-07-29"><hi rendition="#italic">July 29,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis states that the reported audience with the Sultan is gratifying, and
                    that, pending further report promised for Tuesday, <pb facs="0912" n="824"
                        xml:id="pg824"/> the squadron under the command of Admiral Barker will be
                    held in readiness subject to orders. The Government of the United States expects
                    that its wishes will be fully complied with. Instructs him to keep the
                    Department adequately advised.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
